iginChamber":"House","policyArea":"Energy","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"T000469","district":20,"fullName":"Rep. Tonko, Paul [D-NY-20]","party":"D","state":"NY"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2026-02-04","actionDesc":"Reported to House","text":"<p><strong>Weatherization Enhancement and Readiness Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill reauthorizes through FY2030 and modifies the Weatherization Assistance Program. Under the program, the Department of Energy (DOE) provides grants for low-income households to improve the energy efficiency of their homes.</p><p>The bill increases the cap on the average assistance provided per home from $6,500 to $12,000.</p><p>The bill also directs DOE to include in its annual report to Congress a description of the impacts of enhancement and innovation readiness efforts on eligibility for assistance under the program.</p>","updateDate":"2026-03-06T18:08:41Z","versionCode":"07"}],"title":"Weatherization Enhancement and Readiness Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-06-11T23:26:35Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-06-11T23:26:35Z"}
